a little taller than I, pale green, amused eyes.
With her is a young man -- husband, brother, lover, it's not my job.
And she says, "Pardon me, ma'am" -- that's how we talk down there -- "is that your mother?"
I said, "No, I follow little old women around parking lots to see if they'll stop. Yes, it's my mother!"
The boy, now, he says. "Well, what my sister meant" -- they look at each other, it's a knowing glance -- "God, she's crazy!"
I said, , and the young girl and the young boy say, "No, no, honey, we just want to know one more thing."
